    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d540">

                <pb facs="0767" n="667" sameAs="frus:frus1934v01/pg667"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">561.35E1/14: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Geneva</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Gilbert</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Geneva</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1934-01-26T17:00:00+01:00">January 26, 1934—5
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received January 26—1:30 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>24. Secretariat has just received a communication from the International Sugar
                    Council setting forth its views following a meeting in Brussels commencing
                    January 20 wherein American suggestions were considered. The Council’s opinion
                    coincided in substance with that expressed by the British Colonial Office as set
                    forth in my 22, January 25, 2 p.m., paragraph 1, to the effect that while the
                    Council still favors its original suggestions it has no fundamental objections
                    to government representatives from the Chadbourne countries; the Council,
                    however, is strongly opposed to enlarging the representation at the preliminary
                    meeting.</p>
                <p>Stoppani will leave here for London on Monday next to see MacDonald<anchor n="7"
                        xml:id="d540-f1"/> at which time final decisions will probably be made. He
                    would appreciate any further advices respecting the American position which may
                    reach him before he leaves Geneva (my 22, paragraph 2). He will, however, while
                    in London keep in touch with the Secretariat by telephone and Secretariat will
                    keep me informed.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gilbert</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d540-f1" n="7" xml:id="d540-f1-content">
                <p>J. Ramsay MacDonald (British Prime Minister), chairman of the Monetary and
                    Economic Conference.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
